{
  "dom_id": "step-q176853",
  "name": "Question 4",
  "problem": "Consider the following statement.\n\n$5$ belongs to the set of integer numbers.\n\nWhat is the negation of this statement?",
  "worked_solution": "Let's denote the given statement as $P.$\n\nThe symbol \"$¬$\" represents negation. So, our task is to negate the given sentence. \n\nTo negate our plain English sentence, we place the words \"It is not true that\" in front of it. This gives the following:\n\nIt is not true that $5$  belongs to the set of integer numbers.\n\nIn other words, $5$ does *not* belong to the set of integer numbers. Therefore, $¬P$ means the following:\n\n$5$ does **not** belong to the set of integer numbers.\n\nNote that $P$ is **true,** while $¬P$ is **false.**",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
